RESOLUTION NO.
Pate:______
ENTITLED: “A
RESOLUTION
ACKNOWLEDGING
THE
RECEIPT
OF
THE
PRELIMINARY COST MODELS FOR A SECOND LEVEL ON THE
CHEYENNE MUNICIPAL COURT BUILDING TO BE LOCATED AT 308
WEST 17th STREET AND SUPPORTING THE DEDICATION OF FUNDS
TO DESIGN AND BUILD A FINISHED SECOND LEVEL ON THE
CHEYENNE MUNICIPAL COURT BUILDING.”
WHEREAS, on May 2, 2017, voters approved a one percent (1%) Specific Purpose
Sales and Use Tax to raise Nine Million Dollars ($9,000,000.00) for the construction of a new
Municipal Court; and
WHEREAS, on May 14, 2018, the Governing Body approved the purchase of Real
Property located at 308 West 17th Street in the City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming,
through City Contract #6835; and
WHEREAS, on August 22, 2018, the City completed all steps necessary to complete
the purchase of the Real Property; and
WHEREAS, the firm of Noel Griffith Jr. & Associates Architects has been retained
to design the new Municipal Court; and
WHEREAS, at the request of the City, Noel Griffith Jr. & Associates Architecis have
completed Preliminary Cost Models for a Second Level on the Cheyenne Municipal Court
Building, a copy of which is attached hereto as Exhibit A; and
WHEREAS, completing the second story on the Cheyenne Municipal Court Building
will ensure the building’s compatibility with existing two-story structures on the block and in
the immediate vicinity, may assist with adding historical façade elements, and will provide
needed space for municipal operations; and
WHEREAS, a commitment by the Governing Body to move forward with the second
story on the Cheyenne Municipal Court Building is necessary at this time to facilitate
appropriate engineering, structural and design decisions.
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERMNG BODY OF
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING:
1.
Receipt of the Preliminary Cost Models for a Second Level on the Cheyenne
Municipal Court Building is hereby acknowledged; and
2.
The Governing Body states its commitment to dedicate necessary hinds to design
and build a finished Second Level on the Cheyenne Municipal Court Building.
PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this
day of
2018.
Marian J. Orr, Mayor
(Seal)
AHEST:
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk
```

