Re: PRELIMINARY COST MoDELS FOR A SECoND Ln’EL OF THE COURTS BUILDING, 308 WEST 17Th STREET
Dear Vicki,
To address the possibility of adding a second level to the future Cheyenne Municipal Courts Building at 308
West 17th Street, we have been tasked with providing estimated costs associated with this second level as
a shell only and a finished space. With either scenario, there are many variables to consider that will affect
the Project Cost Model for each presented herein. These items may include: the identification and function
of the other tenants in the building, vertical transportation needs, final building square-footage, and
historical façade considerations, among other considerations. These variables will need to be reviewed,
and Project Goals determined, to finalize the Project Budget needed to achieve those goals. The costs
estimates presented at this time are to provide a cost magnitude to evaluate the budget required to achieve
either a 2nd floor shell only or a finished 2” floor.
The square-footage used in both the Shell Only and the Finished 2 Floor Cost Models utilize 14,500 sf,
which is the most conservative, as that is the size of the lot and the largest footprint the building can be,
These Cost Models also incorporate a budget allowance of $500,000 for minimal historical elements on the
floor façades.
Please feel free to contact me if there are any questions or concerns with the Preliminary Project Cost
Models.
Sincerely,
Noel Griffith, Jr. AlA
